items/cor-vector-valued-ftc-and-lipschitz-bound.md:52:[L1] The vector-valued derivative and integral are componentwise: $f'(c)_i = f_i'(c)$, and $f$ is integrable exactly when every $f_i$ is, with $\bigl(\int_a^b f\bigr)_i = \int_a^b f_i$; equality of two elements of $\mathbb{R}^{m}$ is equality of all their coordinates ([[def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral]], [[thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity]]).
