research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-369-## Facts & Assumptions
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-370-
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-371-**Given:** The function $f : [0,1] \to \mathbb{R}^{2}$ with $f_0(t) = t^{2}$ and $f_1(t) = t^{3}$, and the reals $\iota(2), \iota(3), \iota(4), \iota(13)$ ([[def-canonical-natural]]).
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-372-
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-373-[A1] The refuted claim, instantiated at $m = 2$, $a = 0$, $b = 1$: there is $\xi \in (0,1)$ with $f(1)-f(0) = f'(\xi)\cdot(1-0)$, that is $f(1)-f(0) = f'(\xi)$.
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-374-
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-375-[L1] Derivatives of powers: $x \mapsto x^{p}$ is differentiable at every real with derivative $\iota(p)x^{\,p-1}$ for $p \ge 1$ ([[lem-derivative-of-a-power]], [[def-integer-power]], [[def-canonical-natural]]).
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-376-
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md:377:[L2] A vector-valued function is differentiable at a point exactly when each component is, and then $f'(t)_i = f_i'(t)$; equality of two elements of $\mathbb{R}^{2}$ is equality of both coordinates ([[def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral]], [[thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity]], [[def-derivative]], [[lem-standard-basis-of-f-n]]).
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-378-
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-379-[L3] Differentiability implies continuity ([[cor-differentiable-implies-continuous]], [[def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity]], [[thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity]]).
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-380-
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-381-[L4] The Euclidean norm: $\lVert y\rVert_2 = \sqrt{y_0^{2}+y_1^{2}}$ on $\mathbb{R}^{2}$, and $\sqrt{\cdot}$ is the unique nonnegative square root ([[def-p-norms-on-rn]], [[def-euclidean-inner-product]], [[thm-of-square-roots]], [[def-norm-and-normed-space]], [[lem-finite-sum-laws]], [[def-finite-sum]]).
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-382-
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-383-[L5] Canonical naturals are positive and strictly increasing, and carry sums to sums and products to products, so $\iota(2)^{2} = \iota(4)$, $\iota(3)^{2} = \iota(9)$, $\iota(4)+\iota(9) = \iota(13)$ and $\iota(3) \ne \iota(4)$ ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]], [[def-canonical-natural]]).
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-384-
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-385-[L6] Squaring is strictly monotone on the nonnegatives, so square roots compare in the same direction ([[lem-of-square-monotone]]).
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-386-
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-387-[L7] The mean value inequality ([[thm-mean-value-inequality]]) and the algebra of derivatives ([[thm-algebra-of-derivatives]]), together with the interval notation ([[def-interval]]).
--
