research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-67-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-68-**Given:** The sequence $\bigl(x^{(k)}\bigr)$ and the function $f$ above; the abbreviation $g(t) := \lVert f(t)\rVert_2 = \sqrt{1+t^{2}+t^{4}}$ ([[def-p-norms-on-rn]], [[def-euclidean-inner-product]]).
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-69-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-70-[L1] Convergence in $\mathbb{R}^{n}$ for $n \ge 1$ is componentwise ([[thm-componentwise-convergence-and-completeness]] clause 1, [[def-metric-convergence]], [[def-sequence]], [[lem-standard-basis-of-f-n]]).
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-71-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-72-[L2] For every real $\varepsilon>0$ there is $K$ with $1/\iota(K+1) < \varepsilon$; $\iota(k+1)>0$; and $0<u\le v$ gives $0 < 1/v \le 1/u$ ([[cor-archimedean-reciprocal]], [[lem-of-naturals-positive]], [[lem-of-inverse-positive]], [[def-canonical-natural]]).
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-73-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md:74:[L3] The vector-valued integral is componentwise, and $f$ is integrable exactly when each $f_i$ is ([[def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral]], [[def-oriented-integral]], [[def-interval]]).
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-75-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-76-[L4] A continuous function on $[a,b]$ is integrable, and $\int_a^b h = G(b)-G(a)$ for any primitive $G$ of a continuous $h$ ([[thm-continuous-implies-integrable]], [[cor-primitives-of-a-continuous-function]]); polynomial functions are continuous ([[thm-algebra-of-continuous-functions]]) and $x \mapsto x^{p}$ has derivative $\iota(p)x^{\,p-1}$ for $p \ge 1$ ([[lem-derivative-of-a-power]], [[def-integer-power]]).
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-77-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-78-[L5] Monotonicity and linearity of the integral ([[thm-monotonicity-of-the-integral]], [[thm-linearity-of-the-integral]], [[lem-finite-sum-laws]], [[def-finite-sum]]).
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-79-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-80-[L6] $\lVert f(t)\rVert_2$ is integrable on $[0,1]$ and $\bigl\lVert\int_0^1 f\bigr\rVert_2 \le \int_0^1\lVert f\rVert_2$ ([[thm-norm-inequality-for-the-vector-valued-integral]], [[def-norm-and-normed-space]]).
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-81-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-82-[L7] Square roots and squaring: $\sqrt{c}$ is the unique nonnegative $s$ with $s^{2} = c$, and for $a,b \ge 0$, $a \le b$ exactly when $a^{2} \le b^{2}$ ([[thm-of-square-roots]], [[lem-of-square-monotone]]).
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-83-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-84-[L8] Canonical naturals carry sums to sums and products to products and are strictly increasing and positive ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]], [[def-canonical-natural]]).
--
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-110-3.2 By monotonicity of the integral, using that $g$ is integrable, $\int_0^1 g \ge \iota(53)/\iota(45)$. [step 1.4, step 2.3, L5, L6]
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-111-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-112-4.1 So $\bigl\lVert\int_0^1 f\bigr\rVert_2 = \iota(7)/\iota(6) < \iota(53)/\iota(45) \le \int_0^1\lVert f\rVert_2$: the inequality of [L6] holds on this example and is **strict**. [step 3.1, step 3.2, step 1.5, L6] ∎
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-113-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-114-## Remarks
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-115-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-116-- **Why the inequality is strict here.** Equality in [[thm-norm-inequality-for-the-vector-valued-integral]] would require the integrand to point in a fixed direction, and $f(t) = (1,t,t^{2})$ changes direction as $t$ runs over $[0,1]$. That heuristic is not what is proved above: the proof separates the two sides by an explicit numerical bound, which is the only argument available at this point in the reading order.
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-117-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-118-- **The lower bound is deliberately crude.** The inequality $\sqrt{1+u} \ge 1 + u/\iota(3)$ used in step 1.4 holds for $0 \le u \le \iota(3)$ and is far from sharp; it is chosen because it is polynomial, so that step 2.3 is an application of [[cor-primitives-of-a-continuous-function]] and nothing more. The exact value of $\int_0^1\sqrt{1+t^{2}+t^{4}}\,dt$ is not a value this page can name.
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-119-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md:120:- **The sequence and the integral are independent computations**, put in one item because they exercise the two halves of [[def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral]] on the same space. Neither uses the other.
