research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-449-## Remarks
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-450-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-451-- **The codomain $\mathbb{R}^{0}$ is excluded by the standing hypothesis
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-452-  $m \ge 1$, and nothing is lost.** $\mathbb{R}^{0}$ has exactly one element, so
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-453-  every function into it is constant and every ball condition holds trivially;
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-454-  every such map is continuous and every limit is the unique point. That case is
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-455-  true, uninteresting, and not what this page is about. It is also outside the
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-456-  reach of [[lem-metrics-on-rn]], which defines the metrics only for $m \ge 1$.
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-457-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-458-- **The domain may be any metric space, and this matters twice below.** The
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log:459:  derivative of [[def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral]] needs a real
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-460-  domain, so it uses the limit clause; the companion page's function of two real
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-461-  variables needs the domain $\mathbb{R}^{2}$, so it uses the continuity clause.
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-462-  Both are instances of the same definition, and neither introduces a second
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-463-  notion.
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-464-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-465-- **When $m = 1$ the codomain is $\mathbb{R}^{1}$, not $\mathbb{R}$.** These are
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-466-  different sets, $\mathbb{R}^{1}$ being a set of functions $1 \to \mathbb{R}$.
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-467-  The map $\theta : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}^{1}$ sending $t$ to the function
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-468-  with value $t$ at $0$ is an isometric bijection for $d_2$
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.log-469-  ([[def-isometry-and-metric-embedding]]), and under it the notions above become
