research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8813-## Statement
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8814-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8815-Let $m \in \mathbb{N}$ with $m \ge 1$ and let $a, b \in \mathbb{R}$ with $a < b$.
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8816-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8817-1. **Fundamental theorem, second part, in $\mathbb{R}^{m}$.** Let
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8818-   $f : [a,b] \to \mathbb{R}^{m}$ be differentiable at every point of $[a,b]$ as
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log:8819:   a function on $[a,b]$ ([[def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral]]), and
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8820-   suppose $f' : [a,b] \to \mathbb{R}^{m}$ is integrable. Then
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8821-   $$\int_a^b f' \;=\; f(b) - f(a).$$
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8822-2. **A bounded derivative gives a Lipschitz function.** Let
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8823-   $f : [a,b] \to \mathbb{R}^{m}$ be continuous on $[a,b]$ and differentiable at
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8824-   every point of $(a,b)$, and let $M \ge 0$ satisfy
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8825-   $\lVert f'(t)\rVert_2 \le M$ for every $t \in (a,b)$. Then
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8826-   $$\lVert f(t) - f(s)\rVert_2 \;\le\; M\,|t-s| \qquad \text{for all } s,t \in [a,b],$$
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8827-   that is, $f$ is Lipschitz with constant $M$ as a map
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8828-   $([a,b], d_{\mathbb{R}}) \to (\mathbb{R}^{m}, d_2)$
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8829-   ([[def-lipschitz-holder-contraction]], [[lem-real-line-is-a-metric-space]],
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8830-   [[lem-metrics-on-rn]]).
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8831-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8832-## Facts & Assumptions
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8833-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8834-**Given:** A natural $m \ge 1$, reals $a < b$, and a function $f : [a,b] \to \mathbb{R}^{m}$ with the hypotheses of the clause under discussion; points $s, t \in [a,b]$.
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8835-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log:8836:[L1] The vector-valued derivative and integral are componentwise: $f'(c)_i = f_i'(c)$, and $f$ is integrable exactly when every $f_i$ is, with $\bigl(\int_a^b f\bigr)_i = \int_a^b f_i$; equality of two elements of $\mathbb{R}^{m}$ is equality of all their coordinates ([[def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral]], [[thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity]]).
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8837-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8838-[L2] The second fundamental theorem: if $G$ is differentiable on $[a,b]$ with $G' = g$ and $g$ is integrable on $[a,b]$, then $\int_a^b g = G(b)-G(a)$ ([[thm-ftc-second-part]], [[def-derivative]]).
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8839-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8840-[L3] The mean value inequality on a subinterval ([[thm-mean-value-inequality]]): for $s<t$, $f$ continuous on $[s,t]$ and differentiable on $(s,t)$ with $\lVert f'\rVert_2 \le M$ there, $\lVert f(t)-f(s)\rVert_2 \le M(t-s)$.
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8841-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8842-[L4] Restricting the domain of a function preserves a limit and its value, the $\varepsilon$-$\delta$ condition then quantifying over fewer points; in particular if $f$ is differentiable at $c$ as a function on $[a,b]$ and $c$ is a limit point of $[s,t] \subseteq [a,b]$, then the restriction of $f$ to $[s,t]$ is differentiable at $c$ with the same derivative ([[def-function-limit]], [[def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity]], [[def-limit-point-r]], [[def-interval]]).
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8843-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8844-[L5] Norms and the induced metric: $\lVert w\rVert_2 \ge 0$, $\lVert -w\rVert_2 = \lVert w\rVert_2$, and $d_2(u,w) = \lVert u-w\rVert_2$ ([[def-norm-and-normed-space]], [[def-p-norms-on-rn]], [[lem-p-norms-are-norms-and-induce-the-published-metrics]]); $d_{\mathbb{R}}(s,t) = |s-t|$ and $|t-s| = |s-t|$ ([[lem-real-line-is-a-metric-space]], [[lem-of-abs-value]]).
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8845-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8846-[L6] Lipschitz maps: $f$ is Lipschitz with constant $L \ge 0$ when $d_Y(f(x),f(x')) \le L\,d_X(x,x')$ for all $x,x'$ ([[def-lipschitz-holder-contraction]]).
--
